# Firebase service account keys. The console downloads these as
# <project>-firebase-adminsdk-<hash>.json straight into whatever directory you
# are in, which is very easily this one — and this repo is public. The key
# bypasses Firestore rules completely, so a single `git add .` would hand the
# whole bookings collection to anyone. Its value belongs in .env.local as
# FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_KEY, not in a file here.
*firebase-adminsdk*.json
serviceAccountKey.json
service-account*.json

